  "docTitle": "Deploy on Kubernetes (Strimzi) - SDE Prep Dojo",
  "description": "Move the ShopStream Kafka pipeline from Docker Compose to Kubernetes: a 4-node kind cluster, the Strimzi operator running a KRaft Kafka cluster from custom resources, topics as code, probes, PodDisruptionBudgets, NetworkPolicies, a CPU HPA for the API and KEDA scaling the consumer on lag.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n        <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n          <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"4\">Level 4 - Advanced</span>\n          <span class=\"time\">70 min</span>\n          <span class=\"chip k8s\">Kubernetes</span>\n          <span class=\"chip kafka\">Strimzi</span>\n          <span class=\"chip\">KEDA</span>\n        </div>\n        <h1>Deploy on Kubernetes (Strimzi)</h1>\n        <p class=\"lead\">Take the same pipeline you ran with Docker Compose and run it on a real (local) Kubernetes cluster. You will see which process creates each pod, how an operator runs Kafka for you, and why the API scales on CPU but the consumer scales on lag.</p>\n      "
  },
